  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Shivashankar Shripati Bhure vs The State Of Maharashtra And Another on 22 July, 2025 1140.25aba (1) In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Bench At Aurangabad 964 Anticipatory Bail Application No. 1140 Of 2025 Shivashankar Shripati Bhure Versus The State Of Maharashtra And Another .....",
    "facts": "The FIR is lodged on 07/09/2024 at 06:55 hours with the Deoni Police Station, Dist. Latur. The offences are registered under Sections 123, 223, 274, 275, 3(5) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 and under Section 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act. 3. The role ascribed of the present applicant in the FIR is that he was the driver of the vehicle in which alleged contraband found.",
    "arguments": "The Supreme Court has recently 1140.25aba (2) passed an order in Special Leave to Appeal (Cri.) No.8698/2023 in the Shivashankar Shripati Bhure vs The State Of Maharashtra And Another on 22 July, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/159342559/ 1 case of Eknath Bhalchandra Patil Vs. The State of Maharashtra, where the Supreme Court in its order dated 28/07/2023 has categorically observed that the Petitioner therein shall not be arrested in connection with Crime No.354/2022, subject to condition that he shall cooperate with the investigation. The Supreme Court has also observed that the issue regarding applicability of Section 123 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita [Section 328 of the Indian Penal Code] is pending before the Supreme Court.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "The Supreme Court has recently 1140.25aba (2) passed an order in Special Leave to Appeal (Cri.) No.8698/2023 in the Shivashankar Shripati Bhure vs The State Of Maharashtra And Another on 22 July, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/159342559/ 1 case of Eknath Bhalchandra Patil Vs. The State of Maharashtra, where the Supreme Court in its order dated 28/07/2023 has categorically observed that the Petitioner therein shall not be arrested in connection with Crime No.354/2022, subject to condition that he shall cooperate with the investigation. The Supreme Court has also observed that the issue regarding applicability of Section 123 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita [Section 328 of the Indian Penal Code] is pending before the Supreme Court."
  },
